18. Solution

Here's the complete solution:

function App() {
  const cartItems = 3;


  return (
    <div>
      {cartItems > 0 ? (
        <div>
          <h1>You have {cartItems} items</h1>
          <button>View Cart</button>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div>
          <h1>Your cart is empty</h1>
          <button>Continue Shopping</button>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}


export default App;
Let's understand the important part:
cartItems > 0

This is the condition.

For:

cartItems = 3

we get:

3 > 0

which is:

true

Therefore React renders:

<div>
  <h1>You have {cartItems} items</h1>
  <button>View Cart</button>
</div>

If:

cartItems = 0

then:

0 > 0

is:

false

So React renders:

<div>
  <h1>Your cart is empty</h1>
  <button>Continue Shopping</button>
</div>
